esent, with prerequisites already accepted. Native format/build/declaration checks precede this review; the unit is internal and correctly contributes no public catalog result.","id":"topic:composition","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_mean_sub/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_noise/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.integral_norm_le_sqrt/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_noise/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_sqrt_le/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_cross/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_sq/preferred"],"comparison":"beta=0 reduces momentum variance to batch variance and removes the sharpened transient. sigma=0 forces zero noise in the moment bounds. The b=0 batch-sum identity is harmless; division by zero B is excluded where needed.","id":"topic:boundaries","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_mean_sub/preferred"],"comparison":"For B>=1, subtracting y from the average of x_j equals the average of x_j-y. The nonzero B premise justifies dividing by B; this supplies the centered batch identity.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_mean_sub","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_noise/preferred"],"comparison":"At a fixed past-dependent query Y, summing b fresh noises k0 through k0+b-1 preserves measurability/prefix dependence and has squared norm expectation <=b*sigma^2. The statement includes integrability and allows b=0.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_noise","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.integral_norm_le_sqrt/preferred"],"comparison":"For a measurable matrix random variable under a probability measure with integrable squared norm, the norm is integrable and its expectation is <=sqrt(expected squared norm). This is the valid first-moment conversion, not a squared-norm public criterion.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.integral_norm_le_sqrt","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_noise/preferred"],"comparison":"The explicit D0 and momentum recursion under B>=1,0<=beta<1 and W_t depending only on the first tB samples give measurability, dependence through (t+1)B, squared-integrability and variance <=sigma^2/B * (a+(1-a)beta^(2t)), a=(1-beta)/(1+beta). The initialization coefficient is retained.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_noise","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_sqrt_le/preferred"],"comparison":"For 0<=beta<1 and 0<=y<=1, sqrt(a+(1-a)y^2)<=sqrt(a)+beta*y, a=(1-beta)/(1+beta). This sharpened scalar deduction gives beta^(t+1) rather than beta^t and supports the printed source transient coefficient beta/(1-beta).","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_sqrt_le","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_cross/preferred"],"comparison":"Measurable X,Y depend only on the tape prefix before k; X has integrable squared norm. Under the IID stochastic-gradient model, the inner product of X with fresh centered noise at Y is integrable and has zero mean. This is the conditional orthogonality needed in the batch variance proof.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_cross","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_sq/preferred"],"comparison":"For a measurable query Y determined by coordinates strictly before k, IID fresh coordinate k and the unbiased finite-variance oracle imply integrability of squared centered noise and expectation <=sigma^2. The nonanticipation premise is explicit.","id":"declaration:OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_sq","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.noise_cross/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.batch_noise/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_noise/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.integral_norm_le_sqrt/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/OracleTemplate.Muon.momentum_sqrt_le/preferred"],"comparison":"The source noise proof uses measurable past-dependent queries, IID fresh samples, unbiasedness and variance<=sigma^2. Batch variance scales as sigma^2/B; momentum variance keeps the first-step coefficient, and the sharper scalar root estimate yields the source beta transient.","id":"node:DSTOCH","source":["src_293fe077ed407a88295c42d8","src_c2006baa6ea30939f6b9a763","src_bc5f0f02387e648e447be892","src_769acb1dc63ec3a33d05a54d","src_555842d1134266274751bccc","src_60fadde6ad80613d32896e45","src_dc6478c950ca730ea0987c12","src_d02eadaa16a3572f6afee7f9","src_4fa1940db34571e3a7f7fb2d","src_9cc08ee4796eaf54d485652b","src_4b2b38c364168ed4ffbf2578","src_11df7e512043b7f430109d54","src_6cd6624b5f4f11c2ab76bf05"],"verdict":"match"}],"notes":["Packet 3,140,587 bytes is below 64,000,000. Verified 7 immutable full compiler-record hashes."],"reviewer":"reviewer"}
